@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `npm start` to serve the site and `npm test` for automated timing tests.
+
+## Contentful update measurements
+
+The page starts browser-native `interaction-contentful-paint` and `soft-navigation`
+observers. These measure elapsed milliseconds from the initiating user input to
+content appearing on screen, including asynchronous updates. They are separate
+from INP, which measures responsiveness up to the next paint.
+
+Use `window.dailyGrindPaintTiming.supported` to check availability and
+`window.dailyGrindPaintTiming.getReports()` to read the latest 100 reports.
+Subscribe to live reports for an analytics integration:
+
+```js
+window.addEventListener('daily-grind:paint-timing', ({ detail }) => {
+  console.log(detail);
+});
+```
+
+- `interaction-paint`: `interactionId`, `duration` (milliseconds), and `size`
+  (painted area). Each progressively larger contentful paint produces a report;
+  these are candidates, not a count of distinct interactions.
+- `soft-navigation`: destination `url`, `navigationId`, `interactionId`,
+  `fcpDuration`, `lcpDuration` (milliseconds), and `size`. Reports finalize on the
+  next soft navigation, page hiding, or explicit `disconnect()`. A missing LCP
+  candidate is reported as `null`. Paints are correlated by interaction ID, and
+  candidates painted before the URL changed are included.
+
+No reports are sent over the network. Reports contain no DOM references or text.
+Call `window.dailyGrindPaintTiming.disconnect()` to flush and remove observers.
+
+These APIs have limited browser availability. Unsupported entry types are skipped;
+there is no synthetic timing fallback that could be mistaken for an actual paint.
+The current page uses full-document links, so it will only produce soft-navigation
+reports if client-side navigation is introduced. Ordinary navigation is not a soft
+navigation, and interactions that do not paint new content produce no entries.
+
+Implementation reference: [Chrome's soft-navigation measurement documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/soft-navigations).
